31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The grant terms are restrictive, only covering session fees for a year, and the scanning suppliers have unreliable delivery windows that slip for larger clients.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's worrying that the outer wards lost their bus links, and while the roads north of the river close in winter, the community halls there still manage to keep their schedules.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,George,,"The running costs for vehicles were significantly over budget last year, and the grant structure seems to shift the financial burden to the operating budget after the first year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,May,,"Past attempts at digitisation were a mess and left things unindexed, but the partner-run evening groups from six years ago are still going strong. Also, former outreach stops were surprisingly popular.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We have retired tradespeople volunteering for repairs, but no staff are trained to supervise outside facilitators, and the person who certified the power tools has retired.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, it seems we both noticed the grant issue. If the operating budget has to take over after a year, we can't rely on those grants for long-term stability.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@May, if the outreach stops were so popular, maybe we should think about how to bring the library to the people instead of waiting for them to come to us.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, exactly. The funding is shaped in a way that creates a deficit in the second year, regardless of the initial amount. We must avoid any proposal that creates a permanent drain on the operating budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,May,,"@Yumi, I agree. The data shows people want the service, but we should be careful not to repeat the mistakes of the past, like that failed digitisation project.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried that if we start something new, we might not have the staff skills to manage it, especially since we've lost our tool certification expert.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that is a valid point. If we choose a technical project, we need to ensure we aren't relying on a single person's expertise or external contractors who might fail us.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@George, if the vehicle costs were high, does that mean a mobile service would be too expensive, or just that we need better budgeting?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,George,,"It suggests that the current budgeting for vehicles is unrealistic. If we go with a mobile service, we must ensure the funding is sustainable and not just a one-time grant.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,May,,"@Yumi, the popularity of outreach is a strong point, but we should look for a model that is self-sustaining, like those partner-run groups May mentioned.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree with May. If we can find a way to work with partners or volunteers who already have the skills, it would take the pressure off the staff.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I think we have a clear picture now: we need a service that is accessible, doesn't rely on unstable contractors, and doesn't create a long-term financial trap for the operating budget.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree. We need to prioritize the people in the outer wards who can't reach us, but we have to do it in a way that actually lasts.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,George,,We must be cautious about any plan that looks good on paper but fails in practice due to the funding structure or hidden operational costs.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,May,,Exactly. We need a proposal that leverages existing community strengths rather than trying to build something from scratch that we can't maintain.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I just hope we don't pick something that requires specialized supervision we can't provide, or we'll just be stressing the staff even more.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
