54,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Looking at the candidates, the Digital Archive Portal seems risky given the contractor issues and past failures. The Maker Workshop also worries me because of the certification and supervision gaps Daisuke mentioned.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I really like the Mobile Branch Service because it solves the bus link problem for the outer wards, and the outreach data May found shows there is a huge demand for it!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,"The Mobile Branch Service is appealing for access, but the vehicle overruns and the grant structure make it a financial risk. Language Learning Circles seem more sustainable if they follow the partner-run model.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,May,,"I agree with George. The Language Learning Circles mirror those successful partner-run groups from six years ago, making them a much safer and more sustainable bet than the Archive Portal.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried about the Maker Workshop since we have no one to certify the tools, but the Language Learning Circles seem manageable if the partners handle the coordination.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if the Language Learning Circles use partner organizations, it reduces our dependence on internal staff and unstable contractors, which aligns with my concerns about stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, but the Mobile Branch Service is the only one that directly helps the people who can't even get to us! Isn't that our primary mission?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,"It is our mission, Yumi, but a service that collapses in two years because the budget was poorly shaped helps no one in the long run. We need a solution that is fiscally sound.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,May,,"@Yumi, I understand your passion, but the Mobile Branch is a huge operational gamble. The Language Learning Circles can still reach people if we coordinate with those community organizations in the outer wards.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think May is right. If the partners are already in the community, we don't have to worry about the bus links or the tool certification issues.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, I appreciate the goal of accessibility, but the data on road closures and vehicle costs suggests the Mobile Branch is too fragile. The Language Learning Circles offer a more stable framework.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I understand the risks, but I can't ignore the people who are completely cut off. Still, if the Language Learning Circles can actually reach those neighborhoods through partners, I can support that.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,George,,It seems we have reached a consensus. The Language Learning Circles provide the best balance of community reach and long-term financial stability without overextending our staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,May,,I'm glad we're on the same page. It's the only option that learns from our history and doesn't set us up for a future failure.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. It feels like the safest choice for the staff and the most reliable way to help the community.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the most reasonable choice given the constraints we've discussed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'll vote for the Language Learning Circles too, as long as we make sure those outer wards are included!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the only proposal that ensures long-term fiscal sustainability.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for the Language Learning Circles. It's the most sensible way to build on what we know actually works.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for the Language Learning Circles. It's the best way to support the community without overloading our staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
